{"content":"Found the bug: in sqlparse/filters/others.py, SpacesAroundOperatorsFilter._process has an inverted comparison operator (`!=` instead of `==`) in the "insert whitespace after operator" check. This causes it to add a spurious extra space when whitespace already follows the operator (e.g. "foo = bar" -> "foo =  bar"), and to skip adding a needed space when the operator is directly followed by a non-whitespace token (e.g. "foo+100" -> "foo +100" instead of "foo + 100"). I'll fix the condition and verify with the earlier failing examples.","tool_calls":[{"id":"fix_1","name":"replace_text","arguments":{"path":"sqlparse/filters/others.py","old_text":"            nidx, next_ = tlist.token_next(tidx, skip_ws=False)
            if not (next_ and next_.ttype != T.Whitespace):
                tlist.insert_after(tidx, sql.Token(T.Whitespace, ' '))","new_text":"            nidx, next_ = tlist.token_next(tidx, skip_ws=False)
            if not (next_ and next_.ttype == T.Whitespace):
                tlist.insert_after(tidx, sql.Token(T.Whitespace, ' '))"}},{"id":"verify_1","name":"run","arguments":{"command":"python -c "import sqlparse; print(repr(sqlparse.format('foo+100', use_space_around_operators=True))); print(repr(sqlparse.format('foo = bar or baz between 1 and 2', use_space_around_operators=True)))""}}]}

